{"name":"Southern Platyfish","hex":"#d0d34d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"southern","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, facing, situated in, or related to the south.","Of or pertaining to a southern region, especially Southern Europe or the southern United States."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of southerner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/southern"},{"term":"platyfish","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Certain fish of the genus Xiphophorus lacking a sword-like extension of the lower tailfin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/platyfish"}],"entries":[{"title":"Southern platyfish","blocks":[{"text":"The southern platyfish, common platy, or moonfish is a species of freshwater fish in family Poeciliidae of order Cyprinodontiformes. A live-bearer, it is closely related to the green swordtail and can interbreed with it. It is native to an area of North and Central America stretching from Veracruz, Mexico, to northern Belize."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rainbow_wag_platy.jpg/330px-Rainbow_wag_platy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southern_platyfish"},{"title":"Platy (fish)","blocks":[{"text":"Platy is a common name of freshwater fish in the genus Xiphophorus that lack a \"sword\" at the bottom of their tails. This species is a livebearer, similar to other fish of the family Poeciliidae, such as the guppy and molly. Platies are native to the east coast of Central America and southern Mexico."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Rainbow_platy.jpg/330px-Rainbow_platy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platy_(fish)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Xiphophorus_maculatus_young.jpg/120px-Xiphophorus_macula